From 1e5390604e349d27430ea39e4b6c56a2fc9715eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iasnezhkov <iasnezhkov@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 11:41:29 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] v4l2: detile the driver native MTK block CAPTURE format
 to NV12

Measured live on the device (task brief, 23.09): mtk-vcodec-dec_v1
CAPTURE output is always its proprietary block/UFO tiled layout (luma
16x32 tiles, chroma 16x16 tiles, chroma right after luma in a single
plane sized to the driver own fb_sz[0], i.e. width x 32-aligned-height
x 1.5) regardless of what VIDIOC_S_FMT negotiates - stock v4l2_codec2
has no awareness of this and expects the driver to write one of its
own kSupportedOutputFourccs (NV12/YV12/I420/P010 family) straight into
the gralloc-backed C2 graphic block it queues as the CAPTURE buffer.
Queuing the client block directly, as today code does, would hand the
client a block full of tiled garbage interpreted as linear NV12.

Stop importing the pool-allocated block as the CAPTURE buffer. Queue a
separate, internally-owned DMA-BUF (TiledCaptureBufferPool, one per
V4L2 buffer slot, /dev/dma_heap/system with the mtk_mm heaps as
fallback, sized to the driver own reported sizeimage) instead, and
after each DQBUF, detile that buffer CPU mapping into the pool block
CPU mapping (VideoFrame::detileFrom) before handing the frame to the
client. DMA_BUF_IOCTL_SYNC brackets the CPU read of the tiled buffer,
matching tools/rigs/v4l2dec.c, which already proved this exact
approach bit-exact against ffmpeg on 30/30 real device frames.

The conversion itself sits behind a small ImageConverter interface
(common/ImageConverter.h) with one implementation today,
LibyuvImageConverter, wrapping libyuv MM21ToNV12 - the same function
and tile geometry external/libyuv already ships and this driver
output matches exactly (confirmed against source/convert.cc and the
NEON row functions comments). This is the seam a future MDP
hardware-backed converter is meant to replace: same dmabuf-in,
gralloc-mapped-out shape, no change needed above VideoFrame.

Copies: one, CPU-side, tiled dmabuf mapping straight into the gralloc
block mapping libyuv writes NV12 to directly - no bounce buffer.
Scope of this patch: 8-bit single-plane MM21 only, matching what has
actually been measured on the device; the 10-bit tiled families
(MT2110/MT21C10/MT21S10/MT10, part 1.1 of the design doc) would need
a second ImageConverter path and are left for later. The destination
block chroma plane is required to be interleaved (colInc=2, i.e. a
real NV12-shaped YCBCR_420_888 allocation) - detileFrom() fails
cleanly instead of writing garbage if gralloc ever backs it as fully
planar I420 on this device, which part 3 of the design doc already
flagged as unconfirmed and worth a live AHardwareBuffer check.

